      "brief": "ONE atlas, four square cells in a row, in this order: goal, portal, gate, wild. 256×256 a cell, so 1024×256 in all. Transparent background. Unlike every other image here these carry their OWN colour and are NOT tinted — paint them finished. Give each its own dark outline: a mark sits on tiles of several colours and heights, and the outline is what keeps its silhouette. Optional: with no file, or under any of §21's assistive palettes, the board falls back to the drawn-in-code silhouettes and loses nothing.",
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "marks",
          "for": "all four, one atlas",
